        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test(qa): migrate channel streaming evidence to transport flow",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `channel-message-flows` QA scenario linked a mock-only Telegram helper test. It claimed primary `channels.streaming` evidence without running a real gateway turn or observing provider-shaped channel requests, and its helper/test pair duplicated behavior already covered by lower-level Telegram tests.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis migrates the scenario to one transport-native QA flow:\n\n- `QaTransportAdapter.waitForOutboundSequence` exposes sent/edited/deleted lifecycle events without leaking QA-bus or provider-specific syntax into YAML.\n- QA Channel now represents partial replies as editable previews while preserving separate block deliveries, tool-call metadata, and failure cleanup.\n- Crabline Telegram normalizes real `sendMessage`, `editMessageText`, and `deleteMessage` recorder traffic and correlates unambiguous preview/final events by message.\n- The deterministic mock provider streams preview-only text, then exposes the asserted marker only in the completed final response, so a stalled preview cannot satisfy primary evidence.\n- The obsolete 616-line Telegram QA helper/test pair is deleted; focused Telegram draft-stream tests remain in place.\n- The repository `channel-message-flows` skill now runs the flow through QA Channel or Crabline Telegram.\n\nNo taxonomy entries or coverage IDs are added. The scenario claims primary `channels.streaming` and secondary `runtime.delivery`; the old unproven thread and reasoning secondary claims are removed.\n\n## User Impact\n\nQA maturity evidence for `channels.streaming` now comes from a real gateway turn. The same YAML runs through the synthetic QA Channel for local/UI workflows and through the real Telegram plugin against Crabline for provider-shaped transport proof.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `OPENCLAW_HEAVY_CHECK_LOCK_SCOPE=worktree node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/qa-lab/src/providers/mock-openai/server.test.ts extensions/qa-channel/src/inbound.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/qa-transport.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/crabline-transport.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/scenario-catalog.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/scenario-flow-runner.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/scenario-runtime-api.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/suite-runtime-flow.test.ts`\n  - 8 files, 182 tests passed before the final matcher guard.\n- `OPENCLAW_HEAVY_CHECK_LOCK_SCOPE=worktree node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/qa-lab/src/qa-transport.test.ts`\n  - 3 tests passed after adding the thread-event and final-marker false-positive guards.\n- QA Channel scenario:\n  - `OPENCLAW_BUILD_PRIVATE_QA=1 node scripts/run-node.mjs qa suite --provider-mode mock-openai --scenario channel-message-flows --concurrency 1 --fast --channel-driver qa-channel --output-dir .artifacts/channel-message-flows-qa`\n  - Passed with `sent -> edited -> edited -> edited` and primary `channels.streaming` evidence; the final marker first appears in the completed delivery.\n- Crabline Telegram scenario:\n  - `OPENCLAW_BUILD_PRIVATE_QA=1 node scripts/run-node.mjs qa suite --provider-mode mock-openai --scenario channel-message-flows --concurrency 1 --fast --channel-driver crabline --channel telegram --output-dir .artifacts/channel-message-flows-crabline`\n  - Passed with real Telegram `sendMessage -> editMessageText` traffic and `sent -> edited` evidence.\n- `node scripts/crabbox-wrapper.mjs run --provider blacksmith-testbox -- env OPENCLAW_CHECK_CHANGED_REMOTE_CHILD=1 OPENCLAW_CHANGED_LANES_RAW_SYNC=1 corepack pnpm check:changed`\n  - Passed typecheck, lint, import-cycle, and repository guards on Testbox `tbx_01kwjtmwswjkjzeeqaaewfd561` before the final matcher-only tightening; head CI provides the final broad gate.\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --stream-engine-output`\n  - Clean after the final matcher guards: no accepted/actionable findings; confidence 0.86.\n",
        "branch": "dallin/qa-channel-message-flows",
